  "archive_readme": "# Turfgrass irrigation + soil moisture (measured vs modeled)\n\n## Source\nPui Kwan Cheung et al., Identifying the mechanisms by which irrigation can cool urban green spaces in summer, Zenodo, 2024.\nOriginal record: https://zenodo.org/records/10972539\nDOI: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10972539\n\n## Contents\n- Turfgrass_Burnley_MEASURED_Hourly.csv — 3,792 rows: actual experimental field observations, joined to Burnley reference climate station on year+hour; use as primary modeling data.\n- Turfgrass_UTC_MODELED_Hourly.csv — 2,808 rows: UT&C simulation output joined to the forcing climate; do NOT label as real-world measurements.\n- Turfgrass_AllSources_LABELED_Hourly.csv — 6,600 rows, measured+modeled stacked (not duplicate-reduced), explicit DataType for every row.\n- Turfgrass_MEASURED_NextHour_Prediction.csv — 3,788 observed current-to-next-hour pairs. Next-hour soil moisture is the target; split by experiment/year/time rather than random hour to avoid temporal leakage.\n- Turfgrass_Data_Dictionary.csv — column meanings and units.\n- Turfgrass_Quality_Report.json — raw source counts and missingness.\n\n## Dates and experimental coverage\n- 2021-01-21 00:00:00 to 2021-03-02 23:00:00 (984 hours)\n- 2022-01-28 00:00:00 to 2022-03-06 23:00:00 (912 hours)\n- Dates are not two continuous full years; each year covers one summer experiment.\n\n## Critical handling / limitations\n- Original index column named empty string is dropped; row order is preserved. Dates come from original Time column, with no UTC/local clock conversion.\n- All NA and missing values are empty in output, not zero. For Burnley2021 Irrigated there are 48 missing irrigation amount cells; do not assume no irrigation.\n- UTC2022 simulation has first 32 hours of missing soil moisture/energy/ET outputs in EACH 2022 plot; these remain missing.\n- The 12th original file UTC2021-Irrigated_1hour.csv was NOT uploaded; it was not filled in or fabricated. Original source link: https://zenodo.org/records/10972539/files/UTC2021-Irrigated_1hour.csv?download=1\n- UTC model variables are not independent ground truth. Avoid mixing model outputs with observed rows in the same training split without explicit modeling choices.\n- Same-hour irrigation is an observed action, not a reliable label of optimal irrigation; this dataset does NOT directly provide a ground-truth 'water needed' target or field capacity, soil pH, soil salinity, grass species, or Riyadh climate.\n- Rainfall and solar radiation can contain small negative instrumental/model night values. No values were clipped or imputed.\n- Burnley2022-ReferenceClimateStation_1hour.csv has generic column names (no unit suffix); mapping to equivalent 2021 columns assumes same physical units. Verify with dataset documentation before a production deployment.\n- Apparent many-row dataset does not imply many independent seasons or sites. This is one site over two short experiments.\n- The parent dataset's source citation should accompany derivative works.\n",
